# =============================================================================
# What may enter a build context. The backend image builds from the REPO ROOT
# (migrations and db/ have to be reachable), so without this file `docker build`
# uploads the whole tree — including backend/.env with the database password,
# the Azure storage key, the JWT secret and the Gmail app password, and three
# node_modules/.venv trees that make the build slow and the image wrong.
#
# Written as an allow-list, not a list of things to exclude: a file added to the
# repo tomorrow is out unless somebody names it here. That is the property
# worth having — a deny-list only protects against the secrets you thought of.
#
# Deny rules come last so they win: later patterns override earlier ones.
# =============================================================================

# Nothing, to begin with.
*

# --- the backend image needs exactly this much --------------------------------
!backend/
backend/*
!backend/src/
!backend/migrations/
!backend/alembic.ini
!backend/pyproject.toml
# Only the dev stage copies these two; the production stage does not.
!backend/tests/
!db/

# --- and never these, wherever they appear ------------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.log
